# Implementation Plan - Cross-Platform Reminders (Android & Desktop)

Build a complete, reliable, cross-platform Medication & Vital Sign Reminder system for CardioGuard that works seamlessly on **Android** (via Capacitor Local Notifications, firing even when the app is closed) and **Desktop** (via Web Notifications API & In-App Alarms).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Android Permissions & Notification Channels**: On Android 13+, the app will request runtime permission (`POST_NOTIFICATIONS`) when the user adds their first medication or enables reminders in Settings.
> **Exact Alarms**: Alarms will use exact alarm scheduling (`USE_EXACT_ALARM`) to ensure timely delivery on Android even when the phone is locked or closed.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Services

#### [NEW] [src/services/notificationService.ts](file:///c:/Users/adeel/OneDrive/Desktop/CARDIOGUARD/src/services/notificationService.ts)
- Implement unified cross-platform notification engine:
  - **Android (Native)**: Wraps `@capacitor/local-notifications` to schedule exact repeating daily alarms, configure high-importance channels (`cardioguard_med_alarms`), and attach action buttons (*"Mark as Taken"*, *"Snooze 15m"*).
  - **Desktop (Web)**: Uses Browser `Notification` API and Web Audio API for desktop notification toasts and in-app sound chime.
  - **Time Parser**: Parses various time strings (`"08:00 AM"`, `"2:30 PM"`, `"14:00"`, etc.) into exact daily `Date` triggers.
  - **Sync & Cancel Methods**: `scheduleMedicationReminder`, `cancelMedicationReminder`, `syncAllReminders`, `scheduleRefillReminder`, `triggerTestNotification`.
  - **Action Listeners**: Listens for lock-screen notification action button clicks on Android.

